  "caveats": [
    "first-harmonic estimate at the 200.622 kHz clock: the real waveform is a duty-cycle pulse plus the switch-node capacitance charge, so the table is a magnitude, not a waveform",
    "the model has no package inductance, so the switch-node capacitance discharges in about a nanosecond; the peak sample is an artifact and the honest repetitive peak is I(Lr) PEAK",
    "ESR is the model's Rser, not a part specification; ESR at 200 kHz differs from the 120 Hz value",
    "parallel resonance between a bulk electrolytic and ceramics is not modelled",
    "the fault windows do not save I(Cin)/I(Rin), so fault-window input current is unknown",
    "cold-start inrush is not modelled either: the 8 ms cold deck saves other probes"
  ]
}
